// Hex, accuracy mode. Companion RONs hex_evasion.ron/hex_crit.ron cover the
// other two chosen-aspect submodes -- same "each mode is its own compendium
// entry, no in-cast submode selector" shape as eyebite (see
// eyebite_asleep.ron's own comment). Reuses `Bane` directly, already shipped
// as a flat accuracy penalty.
//
// Known simplification: the sheet's "extra necrotic damage on the caster's
// own hits against the hexed target" rider is NOT implemented here. This
// engine has no existing primitive for "caster deals +N damage to a specific
// marked target on every subsequent hit" (the closest shipped analogue,
// `BuffKind::ArdentHunt`'s `MarkEntity` + `CombatRequirement::Target(uid)`
// combo, is authored on the ATTACKER's own buff and would need real new
// wiring to instead read off a debuff carried by the DEFENDER) -- building
// that is real, non-trivial plumbing beyond a content-only spell batch.
// Shipping the disadvantage-only mechanic now; the necrotic-on-hit rider is a
// documented follow-up.
BasicRanged(
    energy_cost: 30.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.2,
    projectile: (
        kind: Simple,
        attack: Some((
            damage: 5,
            buff: Some((
                kind: Bane,
                dur_secs: 60,
                strength: Value(0.7),
                chance: 1.0,
            )),
            damage_kind: Necrotic,
        )),
    ),
    projectile_body: Object(BoltFire),
    projectile_speed: 55.0,
    num_projectiles: Value(1),
    meta: (
        school: Some(Enchantment),
        source: Some(Arcane),
        // level 1 spell -> min_level 6, same `level * 6` convention.
        requirements: (min_level: Some(6)),
    ),
)
